    "title": "Over 100 gallons of diesel spill after sedan crashes into big rig on I-880 in Oakland, CHP says - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Aaron Tolentino ,\n2 hours ago\n( KRON ) — Approximately a total of 150 gallons of diesel spilled on I-880 in Oakland Wednesday afternoon, according to the California Highway Patrol (CHP). Around 1:30 p.m., authorities responded to a crash between a gray Honda Accord and a big rig on the northbound on-ramp at Fruitvale.\nThe driver of the Honda had minor injuries and did not require transport to a hospital, CHP said. The big rig was carrying the gallons of diesel at the time of the crash. About 75 gallons spilled on the roadway, and the other 75 spilled in a storm drain.\nSouthwest Airlines to begin service at this small North Bay airport The northbound I-880 offramp at Fruitvale will be closed until 12:01 a.m., Caltrans said.\nCHP did not say whether or not the driver of the big rig was hurt.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KRON4.",
